TEMP HttpRequest.registerCleanup?: (cleanup: InvocationCleanup) => void is unchanged S1.

Public selection remains registerCleanup contract: caller abort exact reason >
selected execution rejection > cleanup failure (single unchanged, multiple aggregate).
Local thrown IO identity is independent of public outcome. Normal close does not abort
or later retroactively abort the local signal. AbortController.abort(undefined) defaults
its reason; no literal-undefined native-abort claim. No competing precedence API.
Owned code MUST preserve its primary using an explicit failed boolean and captured value;
await close with both outcomes observed, rethrow primary if present, else cleanup failure.
The same registered close promise leaves secondary failure visible to invocation drain.
Never use blanket finally-close-masks-primary or unconditional catch-to-success.
Direct hosts may omit registration; close remains required and cleanup-only rejects.

Synchronous registration precedes admission. Parent close closes admission and cooperative
children, sharing settlement. Child close is independent. No opaque handler wait/lease.
Known cat/curl enroll; arbitrary commands opt in. No prebuffer or demand gate. Operation
does not return borrowed stdin or abort sibling/file/stderr; top-level ownership unchanged.
Known stdout closure allows no write attempt but must retain requested writeout's existing
status/error semantics. Required file/header and independent stderr work remain separate.
